of most cacti where water storage takes place. Most species of cacti have lost true leaves, retaining only spines, which are highly modified leaves. As well as defending against herbivores, spines help prevent water loss by reducing air flow close to the cactus and providing some shade. In the absence of true leaves, cacti's enlarged stems carry out photosynthesis."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Various_Cactaceae.jpg/330px-Various_Cactaceae.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cactus","wikidata":"Q14560"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Singapore_Botanic_Gardens_Cactus_Garden_2.jpg/500px-Singapore_Botanic_Gardens_Cactus_Garden_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Singapore_Botanic_Gardens_Cactus_Garden_2.jpg/1280px-Singapore_Botanic_Gardens_Cactus_Garden_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Singapore_Botanic_Gardens_Cactus_Garden_2.jpg/500px-Singapore_Botanic_Gardens_Cactus_Garden_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASingapore_Botanic_Gardens_Cactus_Garden_2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Cactus1web.jpg/500px-Cactus1web.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Cactus1web.jpg/500px-Cactus1web.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACactus1web.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Barrel_cactus_with_a_view.JPG/500px-Barrel_cactus_with_a_view.JPG?utm_sour